WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.334
-Thank you so much for
coming back on the show.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.234
I appreciate it.
-I'm excited.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.834
I know Brianne and Antonia,
right?

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:11.434
I saw, when I drove in, someone
wanted to meet them.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.200
And I had to roll
the window down

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.133
and let them down pretty badly.

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:17.968
She had --
They wanted a picture.

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:19.634
-Oh, someone on the street.
-Someone on the street

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:22.968
was hoping it wasn't me
in that car.

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:27.567
It was, like, right when I went
in, and I just rolled the window

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:30.234
down and I was like -- I said,
"I'm sorry."

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.100
And then I just rolled it
back up.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.701
-They didn't even take picture.

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:34.000
-No.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.033
One of the first times I ever
did a late night --

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.601
like an old "Conan,"
a long time ago.

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:39.801
But I remember I pulled up

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:41.968
and they take pictures of people
when you walk in.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.000
And so, I pull up in the thing

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.601
and all these people walk over
to take a picture.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.868
And then they -- I come out

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:50.901
and they were like,
"We don't know who this is."

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.100
And they all just --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.067
They all walked away.
No one even took --

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.701
It's all digital cameras. They
could just delete the picture.

00:00:56.701 --> 00:01:00.267
[ Laughter ]
They did not want to waste --

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.367
-Hard drive space.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:03.734
-"I don't want to go through
all that.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.534
I don't want to delete it."
-That's a lot of business.

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:07.501
-They just go,
"Nah, never mind."

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.634
-Never mind. We're all good.
-Sorry.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.467
-But you're on the road
constantly.

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:14.267
-Yes.
-And I thank you for stopping in

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:16.133
and doing "The Tonight Show."
What's it like?

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.000
Is the road the same?
Has it changed?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.334
-Yeah, it's the same.
It's, you know, a lot of hotels.

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:22.968
Stay in a lot of hotels.
Some hotels are great.

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:24.501
Some are, like, fine.

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:27.567
I stayed in one, because no one
really works at hotels anymore.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.601
And, like, you go to some of
these small towns.

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:31.968
And it's, like, the guy that
owns it

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:34.133
works there and that's it.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.968
And so, you're like, "Is the
room going to get cleaned?"

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:37.534
And he's like, "No.
I mean, it's not --"

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.200
-He just right straight-out
tells you no.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.234
-Immediate. "No, dude.

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:44.968
We do it every third guest."

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:48.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.734
I called down. One night, there
was a stain on the bed.

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:51.934
And I called and I said, "Hey,

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.701
there's a pretty big stain
on the bed."

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.434
And he goes, "How big is it?"

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.834
I was like, "Dude, I'm about to
get talked into this stain."

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:02.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:05.300
And I was, like, "I don't know,
like 70 nickels' worth."

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.801
I didn't know
how to describe it.

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:10.234
I was like, "If you dropped 70
nickels on the bed, it's that."

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.767
And he was like, "It's not that
bad, to be honest."

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.133
And I was, like, "Alright.
Maybe it's the cleanest room.

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:17.334
Maybe it was a thousand nickels
before I got here."

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.300
-Yeah. 70 nickels is pretty big.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.267
-If you drop 70 nickels,
it's a good spot.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:25.300
-Yeah. "Hello World" is the name
of the special.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.000
What's the significance behind
that?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.567
-Well, I wanted a nice greeting.

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:33.267
I just wanted to do something
that was, like, very warming

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.067
and try to be -- The special
is very fun.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:38.467
It's also a nod to Tiger Woods.

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.501
-Oh.
-When Tiger turned pro

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:43.000
when he was 18, there's a big --
like he said, he goes,

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.267
"Well, hello, world," and makes
a famous, like, thing.

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:49.033
So it was kind of like
it's a mix of --

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.901
I'm a big golfer, big Tiger fan.
-Yeah.

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:54.267
-And so it kind of worked.
I was like, "Oh."

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:55.634
And it's like a little nod
to him.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:57.434
-Yeah.
You actually met Tiger Woods.

00:02:57.434 --> 00:02:58.667
-I actually got to meet him.

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:02.701
I did a show for the PGA,
and he was there.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:05.667
And I told him.
I told him I was naming

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:08.467
this special --

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:12.834
This was a big deal --
This was it.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:16.234
-Judging by this photo, I'm not
sure you did meet Tiger Woods.

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:17.334
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:19.601
-Did you talk to each other?
-Yeah.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:21.067
-Neither one of you are looking
at each other.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.534
-Yeah. They grabbed him.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.367
-Is this at the beginning of
the conversation or is this

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.100
the end when it's awkward
silence like,

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.701
"Someone get me out of here"?
-He didn't know I was there.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:30.934
I just went there and I stood
next to him and just looked

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:33.534
like, "Hey, we're just two buds
hanging out."

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:35.701
-You didn't even get that close
to him.

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:37.467
-You don't want to touch him.
I mean, I don't --

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:40.167
It's Tiger Woods.
-It is Tiger Woods.

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:41.267
You want to give him his space.

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.267
-I told him within eight words,

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:46.234
I told him I was naming my
special after him

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:47.601
saying "hello, world."

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:49.367
It was a lot for him to take in.

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:50.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.601
-Did he react?

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:54.934
-He was like, "Oh, that's cool."
I don't know how to react.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.767
There's no context
to any of this.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.968
He doesn't, like --
He doesn't know me,

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:00.801
doesn't know what I've done.
I'm just walking up like,

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.767
"I'm going to name my comedy
special after you."

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:05.167
And he's like, "Alright."

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:07.667
He goes, "I appreciate it, man."
I was like, "Yeah."

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.200
He talked about you.
-He did?

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.033
-Yeah. Because he said --
I said I was a comic.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:14.000
And he loved coming on here
and just talked about coming on

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.901
the show with his caddie
and just told --

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.834
and just kept talking.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.300
Enough that I was like,
"Alright."

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.968
I go, "That's --" I go --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:22.133
-"I'm not here to talk about
Jimmy Fallon."

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:23.834
-I go, "We've all done
the show, alright?"

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:25.868
[ Laughter ]
-Whatever, Tiger.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:28.300
Let's get out of there.
He's a good dude.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.467
But you do this hour
of new material

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:33.367
and already you're working on
another new material.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:35.300
-Yeah.
-How do you do it?

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.801
You're brilliant.
What is the process?

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:40.901
-Yeah, I'm brilliant.
-Sorry, I snuck that in there.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:42.701
-Yeah, I liked it.
-I know.

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:46.000
You're a pretty humble guy. You
don't like people saying that.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.167
-That's what we wrote down.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:48.534
I go, "Make sure you say
brilliant."

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:50.234
-Yeah, it says here --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:52.334
-Yeah. You just think of --
I don't know.

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:53.467
You think of dumb stuff.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:55.067
-What kind of stuff are you
thinking of now?

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:57.667
-One, so I thought about
the old times.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:01.033
Because cars now, if you drove
a car here,

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.567
if you drove a car somewhere,
remember you leave your lights

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.300
on and someone's like, "Who's
got a Honda Accord?

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.767
Your lights are on."
-Yeah.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:09.334
-But back in the old days,
it was horse and buggies.

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:11.767
So they would park their horses.

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:14.067
And they were like, "Alright,
who's got a brown horse?"

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:15.200
And that's everybody.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.734
Everybody's like,
"I think we all do."

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:19.167
And then, it's like,
your horse is gone.

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:20.767
It's just gone.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:25.501
That would be their lights,
is your engine is gone.

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:29.100
And then you got -- They'd be
like, "Did you look for it?"

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.434
And you got a lantern.

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:33.734
You're like, "We looked as much
as a lantern would look.

00:05:33.734 --> 00:05:37.167
Like, it was never within
six feet of us."

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:38.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.434 --> 00:05:40.033
-This is stuff that you're
thinking of right now.

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:42.033
-This is the prime stuff

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:43.267
you're going to see out there
on the road.

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:44.901
[ Laughter ]
I'll tell you what.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:47.501
-No. Come on.
-These are the hits.

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.868
-Last time, you said you're
going to cut down on sugar

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:52.467
and get into healthy --
You look fantastic.

00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:54.634
-Thank you. It's gotten better.

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:56.834
I still have just meltdowns

00:05:56.834 --> 00:05:59.200
where I'll still go to
McDonald's.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.434
Went through a McDonald's, and I
had to open my door one time

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:04.601
because my window was broke.
That was pretty sad.

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:07.501
[ Laughter ]
That's sad for me and them.

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:10.234
It's like me and the McDonald's
worker are all just like,

00:06:10.234 --> 00:06:12.167
"What are we doing with our --"
They shouldn't see

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:15.033
your whole body in a
drive-through window.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:17.534
They shouldn't -- Like, you just
have to open it.

00:06:17.534 --> 00:06:19.501
And you're like -- And you just
take all the --

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:22.634
They see your shoes.
And you're like --

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:24.200
You're like,
"I don't know, dude.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.501
I should've just not done it."

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:27.601
The one day my window doesn't --

00:06:27.601 --> 00:06:31.634
My window goes down every day
on Earth of my life.

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:33.367
And the one day it doesn't,
I'm like,

00:06:33.367 --> 00:06:34.834
"I'll probably do
a drive-through today."

00:06:34.834 --> 00:06:36.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.334 --> 00:06:37.767
-You're a glutton for
punishment, man.

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:39.234
That's terrible.
-It's brutal.

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:42.067
-That's terrible.
-But I have gotten better.

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:43.400
I'm 43.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.300
43, you still think
you're young.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.367
You know, like, I'll hang out
like a 23-year-old.

00:06:47.367 --> 00:06:48.567
And I'm like, "You get it, dude.

00:06:48.567 --> 00:06:50.601
We're just a couple young dudes
kicking it."

00:06:50.601 --> 00:06:51.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.734 --> 00:06:53.501
And some guy will be like,
"I'm 45."

00:06:53.501 --> 00:06:55.234
I'm like, "Beat it, old man!"

00:06:55.234 --> 00:06:56.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.868 --> 00:07:00.534
"I can't believe that guy had
the nerve to hang out.

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:03.200
You know?
Let's go sit down a little bit."

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.934 --> 00:07:09.834
I went and got a physical
recently.

00:07:09.834 --> 00:07:12.300
And after your 40s,
I'll tell you --

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:16.067
Before 40, you go through, like,
a drive-through window.

00:07:16.067 --> 00:07:18.734
They're just, like, you move
your neck, and they're like,

00:07:18.734 --> 00:07:20.734
"Come on, man, you're wasting
everybody's time, alright.

00:07:20.734 --> 00:07:23.501
Go live a life."
And then you pass 40,

00:07:23.501 --> 00:07:25.968
and the doctor's like, "You mind
shutting that door behind you?"

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.167 --> 00:07:31.234
He's like, "I'd lock it.
We're about to get after it."

00:07:31.234 --> 00:07:33.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.834 --> 00:07:37.567
And it was the first time
I've ever been talked to old.

00:07:37.567 --> 00:07:39.167
And so, it was just me and him.

00:07:39.167 --> 00:07:41.067
And he goes, "Do you pee a lot
at night?"

00:07:41.067 --> 00:07:43.901
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:46.801
And I was like, "Did my dad just
walk in the room?"

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:49.901
Like, how old -- I never peed at
night in my life.

00:07:49.901 --> 00:07:51.133
I was like, "How about that?

00:07:51.133 --> 00:07:52.634
I don't pee till
the sun goes down."

00:07:52.634 --> 00:07:54.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:57.400
But I was like, "Just so I know,
what is a lot?

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:58.801
What is a big amount?"

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:01.467
And I tell you what.

00:08:01.467 --> 00:08:04.400
He's ruined me.
I only pee at night now.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:05.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.868 --> 00:08:07.634
I would love to pee
during the day.

00:08:07.634 --> 00:08:09.968
My body's like, "Enjoy the day.

00:08:09.968 --> 00:08:12.200
We'll get it out tonight.
Don't worry about it. Have fun."

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.567
[ Laughter ]
-Nate Bargatze, everybody.

00:08:14.567 --> 00:08:17.801
His new special
"Nate Bargatze: Hello World"

00:08:17.801 --> 00:08:21.334
comes to Prime Video one week
from today.

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:22.701
Congratulations.

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:24.567
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show."

00:08:24.567 --> 00:08:26.300
Nate Bargatze, come on!

